WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.910 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Where could floodwater go?

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.450 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
TerraScope follows the Gandak River
in Bihar.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.132 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
A planner can replay a storm,
then pick a place to survey.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.836 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The replay starts on 28 September 2024.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.680 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Watch the river reading change
by 2 October.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.029 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
ERA5 reconstructs rainfall.
GLOFAS models river flow.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.620 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Near Sonepur, the map flags low spots
in the terrain.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.540 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Each one gives a field team
a place to investigate.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.010 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Open a candidate to see its footprint.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.320 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The estimate is the volume
up to the spill rim.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.670 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
How much water it can actually hold
is still unknown.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.330 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
This cross-section shows the dip
and its rim.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.050 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
A ground survey can check the outlet
and how the site drains.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.929 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The student behind TerraScope asked
an AI agent to deploy it with Embarko.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.060 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The prompt shown here
is a reconstruction.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.910 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The result is a public link.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.450 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Open TerraScope at the address
on screen.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.010 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Replay the storm and choose a site
to investigate.
